# S. Sergeev, H. Schneider and P. Butkovic, visualization scaling (2009)

Bibliography label: Sergeev--Schneider--Butkovic 2009.

Published source: S. Sergeev, H. Schneider and P. Butkovic,
*On visualization scaling, subeigenvectors and Kleene stars in max algebra*,
Linear Algebra and its Applications 431(12) (2009), 2395--2406.
DOI: `10.1016/j.laa.2009.03.040`.

The paper studies diagonal similarity scalings in max algebra, including
strict visualization in which noncritical entries become strictly smaller
than the maximum cycle mean. This is the standard neighbouring language for
positive vertex gauges and critical graphs. The project's graphwise
max-affine system also carries additive shifts and optional floors, so its
gauge theorems are not asserted to be instances of every matrix theorem in
the paper.

This file is a source-positioning note. It states no Lean version of the
paper's scaling results.
